[["**", -0.07681050151586533], ["**.", -2.6132733821868896]]}, {"t": " (", "lp": -0.7175756096839905, "top": [[" (", -0.7175756096839905], [" for", -1.4269566535949707]]}, {"t": "one", "lp": -0.922989547252655, "top": [["one", -0.922989547252655], ["ic", -1.6367595195770264]]}, {"t": "API", "lp": -0.3754376769065857, "top": [["API", -0.3754376769065857], ["D", -2.0338258743286133]]}, {"t": " \"", "lp": -1.4754793643951416, "top": [[" \"", -1.4754793643951416], [" D", -1.802029013633728]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -0.1472133994102478, "top": [["ic", -0.1472133994102478], ["IC", -3.6181588172912598]]}, {"t": "x", "lp": -0.018184736371040344, "top": [["x", -0.018184736371040344], ["X", -4.80645751953125]]}, {"t": "\").", "lp": -0.07756756991147995, "top": [["\").", -0.07756756991147995], ["\",", -3.0508341789245605]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which aren't on the default PATH.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives (the git clone). |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go (out-of-source build). |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, minimal syntax) instead of Make. |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Compile with **optimizations** (`-O3`-level) and no debug symbols. |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where `make install` will place files (standard system location). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Put libraries in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`). |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C compiler** (oneAPI \"icx\")."}